#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0169 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: The value of CNSR is not a positive integer or 0
#note "Added 2026-09-14 (PLAN-column-type-conformance carried-forward). The Check is a disjunction — `not is_integer(CNSR) or num(CNSR) < 0` — and until this file only the SIGN arm ran: the -invalid- pair uses -1 and 0, both integers, so `not is_integer` was false on every row ever fixtured while BOTH arms were rewritten by the plan. Row 1 is a non-integer that is POSITIVE, so it can only fire through the is_integer arm; row 2 is a conformant 0 and must not fire, which is what keeps the count meaningful if the arm ever starts firing on everything."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 CNSR=1.5
# Declared-tier scope: structure= states the ADaM data structure this minimal table stands for;
# #define is its mandatory carrier (ScenarioDeclaredScopeProvider.install).
#define standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col CNSR type=Num
---
1.5
0
---
